aws-load-balancing is the AWS Elastic Load Balancing (ALB / NLB / GWLB) configuration and operations
skill in the load-balancer family (PR 2 of 2). The design and platform-selection decision lives in
load-balancer-selection (PR 1). Skill licensed MIT (the primary-source licence). AWS Classic ELB is
legacy and out of scope.

Boundary with adjacent AWS skills (no duplication):
  - aws-networking-audit owns the VPC-side security review of the load balancer (security-group rules,
    ENI/subnet placement, public-exposure audit, NACLs). It already defers ALB/NLB configuration content
    to this skill; this skill defers exposure auditing back to it. Reciprocal, clean boundary.
  - aws-cloud-ops owns broader AWS service-selection and cost framing; it already defers load-balancer
    depth to this skill. Reciprocal.
  This skill resolves the forward-refs both of those carried ("the load-balancer families") with no
  back-edit.

